 The Questionnaire is the essential tool for data
collection of a census. As all the previous
censuses are conducted manually, their
questionnaires are paper-based. However, since
the Population and Housing Census 2022 are
conducted following the CAPI method, its
questionnaire is designed keeping digital platform
in consideration. In the case of designing  the
census questionnaire, at first, a team in the project
is formed to develop its first draft keeping the
questionnaire of the last census 2011 and other
relevant issues in consideration. Later on, it is
thoroughly reviewed and analysed in a number of
consultation meetings organized at BBS level,
and made necessary changes. In order to make
the questionnaire more inclusive, a number of
consultation workshops are organized with the
participations of representatives from various
ministries/ divisions/agencies, academics,
researchers, civil society members, media
personnel, experts and other stakeholders.
Incorporating the comments and suggestions
received through the workshops, the revised draft
of the questionnaire is prepared.  Subsequently, it
is further systematically reviewed and analysed
by the ‘Technical Support Team’ for med by the
SID to accomplish technical activities of the
census, and followed by the ‘Professor’s Forum’
formed with some renowned professors of
different universities. After that, the questionnaire
is pre-tested in the field to observe its
performance. In light of the experiences and
findings gathered from the pre-test, the final draft
of the questionnaire is prepared. Afterwards, its
CAPI version is developed to carry out data
collection of the census digitally, using digital
device tablets, following the Computer Assisted
Personal Interviewing (CAPI) method, and a field
test is conducted in every division to assess the
performance of the CAPI questionnaire.  After
incorporating the findings of the test in the CAPI
version, again a pretest is conducted in 821
selected EAs across the country. Based on the

